In America, the word is sometimes applied as a slur to African-
Americans.
(Variations include "porch monkey" and "jungle monkey").

http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?page=5&term=monkey
(definition 30)
http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=jungle+monkey
(definition 1)
http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=porch+monkey
(definition 2)

However, actual monkeys are very well known for a propensity to steal
things.

I believe the origin of the use of the word as a bigoted slur is
because
African-Americans are perceived (by bigots) to have a similar
propensity,
as well as a comment on the fact that their ancestry derives from
the countries of Africa, much of which is jungle and where many
species of monkey and ape dwell.

I personally find the epithet very distasteful. However, I do not
think
the DevTeam meant this in a racist way; I think it is related more
directly to the behavior of actual monkeys, and the unfortunate
coincidence with the use of the slur is attributable to the fact that
both the Nethack concept of monkeys and the origin of the bigoted
slur BOTH derive from observations of actual monkey behavior.


